<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 11.50 trln rbls paper April 23.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 11.50 trln rbls paper April 23.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will auction 7.50 trillion roubles of 364-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 23005) and 4.00 trillion roubles in an additional 707-day tranche of the two-year bonds maturing March 1999 (series 24011) on April 23, the Central Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>    Series number		   23005</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denomination		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor			     364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   April 22, 1998</p>
<p>    Series number		   24011 (additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denomination		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Original issue date	   April 2, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	     707 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   March 31, 1999</p>
<p>    First coupon date	     October 1, 1997</p>
<p>Coupon size 37.45 pct (186,737 roubles)</p>
<p>The first coupon includes accruals of 21,546.58 roubles.</p>
<p>On April 23 the Finance Ministry will also repay 6.91 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of 182-day T-bills (series 22055).</p>
<p>It will also pay 246.86 billion roubles in interest on the two-year OFZ interest-bearing government bond (series 24009) maturing October 1998.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
